On Tue, 9 Feb 2010, Jon "Top Hat" Jones wrote:

> One thing I want to mention: {la} is not only for cmene. It is the gadri
> used for all cmevla. {la mlatu}, for instance, is a cmevla, whereas
> {la.aionys.} is a cmene.

I think you have it backwards.  {cmevla} is the term for lojban words that end
in consonants, and can only be used as names ({.aionys.}, for instance).
{cmene} is any lojban name, including cmevla and selbri used as names (for
instance, {zo xalbo mi cmene}).

